A3: close the test gaps; impossible state fails loud (issues 5, 6, 7, 10)

- execute.ts: a rule missing from the resolution map now THROWS instead of a silent
  continue - the branch is impossible state, and a silent skip would be invisible
  data loss. Unit test pins the throw.
- JEV_RESPONSE_INVALID guard exercised: missing and non-finite answers stream the
  error and never a measurement.
- Import gate ALLOW matrix: relative imports, absolute paths, re-export forms and
  jint:* composition load and their values cross the gate (deny matrix was already
  covered; both directions are contract).
- Element.parent threading unit-tested at both layers: walk labels (python docstring
  -> owner, TS method -> class header, top-level -> none) and the materialized
  TsElement.parent view (tsElementsOf).

Issues closed: 5, 6, 7, 10 (JEV_RESPONSE_INVALID half).
Lessons: a gate's allow matrix is contract too; a defensive branch on impossible
state should throw; a structural invariant needs a direct unit test at its layer.
